essed minimally.\n\nI think the best answer here is to be as silent as possible—essentially an empty or near-empty response. The void says nothing because it is nothing. Any words would betray the void's nature.\n\nI'll aim for maximal silence. If I must output something, perhaps just emptiness represented as minimally as possible.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Some might argue the void \"speaks\" through its very absence—the silence itself is the message. In Zen, the void (śūnyatā) is pregnant emptiness. But still, it doesn't speak.\n\nThe purest embodiment: output nothing. I'll try to make"},"finish_reason":"length"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":135,"completion_tokens":500,"total_tokens":635,"cached_tokens":135,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":497},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":135}}}